                           <td>The PSA level is significantly elevated above the normal range for females. As PSA is not typically present at high levels in women, this result may indicate a laboratory or sample identification error, or rarely, a non-prostatic source such as certain tumors. Clinical correlation and repeat testing are strongly recommended to rule out pre-analytical or analytical issues.</td>
